    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 all 21 tests pass, including the new Cp12 (address normalization), the changed Cp10 (household-duplicate) and Cp11 (shared household id), and no regressions elsewhere.\n\n## What I changed\n\nAddress normalization is now applied on the one create path, `POST /api/owners`.\n\n1. **New `AddressNormalizer` helper** (`rest/function/owner/AddressNormalizer.java`) \u2014 canonical normalization: trim, collapse internal whitespace to single spaces, upper-case, and whole-token abbreviation expansion (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). Idempotent; `null`/whitespace-only \u2192 `\"\"`.\n\n2. **`ValidateOwnerFields`** \u2014 normalizes the address and writes it back onto the request *before* the required-field checks. Because it runs first, a whitespace-only address becomes blank after normalization and is rejected as an `address` 400. Since `BuildOwner` maps this request into the owner, the normalized value is what gets stored and returned.\n\n3. **`RejectDuplicateHousehold`** and **`AssignHousehold`** \u2014 address comparisons (and the household-id derivation) now use `AddressNormalizer.normalize(...)`, so duplicate detection and the shared `householdId` are computed from the normalized form. Last-name comparison keeps its existing lower-case normalization.\n\nThe effect verified by tests:\n- `\"  12  main  st \"` \u2192 returns `\"12 MAIN STREET\"`; `\"7 elm ave\"` \u2192 `\"7 ELM AVENUE\"`; `\"   \"` \u2192 400.\n- `\"12 Main St\"` vs `\"12  main  street\"` now collide as the same household (409).\n- `\"12 Main St\"`, `\"12 main street\"`, `\"12  MAIN  ST\"` resolve to the same `householdId`.",
